// Definite assignment is a real flow merge, not "any assignment anywhere": a lone `if` may be skipped, so
// the value is not assigned on every path that reaches the return. The rule lives on the `out` PARAMETER,
// which is the thing that promises to be filled; a `slot` LOCAL never needs the merge, because its own
// fill must be unconditional. (Both arms assigning IS accepted — see tests/out_param_paths.kama.)
fn void pick(bool c, out int32 x) {
    if (c) { x = 1; }      // only one path assigns
}                          // ERROR: 'x' not assigned on every path before this function returns
fn int32 main() { slot int32 v; pick(c: true, x: out v); return v; }
